%U A361622 8986,9599,10224,10877,11550,12235,12932,13665,14418,15191,15968,16781,17606,18459,19324
%N A361622 Number of distinct circles that can be constructed from a point on the origin and n equally spaced points on each of the +x,-x,+y,-y coordinates axes using only a compass.
%C A361622 A circle is constructed for every pair of the 1 + 4n points, the first point defines the circle's center while the second the radius distance.
%C A361622 See A354605 and A353782 for images of the resulting vertices and regions.
%C A361622 From _Martin Fuller_, Oct 18 2026: (Start)
%C A361622 Let T(n,k) = the number of circles centered at (k,0) = |{j^2 : j = 1..n+|k|} u {j^2 + k^2 : j = 1..n}|.
%C A361622 T(n,k) for k > 0 is bounded by 2n + k - A046079(k) <= T(n,k) <= 2n + k, with equality on the left for all sufficiently large n (depending on k).
%C A361622 The current sequence a(n) = n + 4 * Sum_{k=1..n} T(n,k) = n(10n+3) - 8*(number of Pythagorean triangles with both legs <= n).
%C A361622 (End)
%F A361622 a(n) = n(10n+3) - 8 * #{m : A009012(m) <= n}. - _Martin Fuller_, Oct 18 2026
%o A361622 (PARI) a(n) = n*(10*n+3) - 8*sum(b=1, n, sum(c=b+1, sqrtint(2*b^2), issquare(c^2-b^2))); \\ _Martin Fuller_, Oct 18 2026
%Y A361622 Cf. A354605 (vertices), A353782 (regions), A356358 (edges), A361623 (k-gons).
%Y A361622 Cf. A046079.
%K A361622 nonn,changed
%O A361622 1,1
